      {
        "key": "b",
        "label": "(b)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 8,
          "ms": 15
        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Some domestic cats have no tails (tailless). The tailless phenotype in cats is genetically controlled.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fig. 3.1 shows a tailless cat.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "figure",
            "id": "fig3.1",
            "caption": "Fig. 3.1",
            "src": "figures/q3_fig3_1.png",
            "alt": "Copyright placeholder for the cat photograph",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A small population of domestic cats, including some tailless cats, was introduced to an island called the Isle of Man in the 1700s.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "After several generations, without artificial selection from humans, a high proportion of the cat population was tailless.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Suggest why the tailless phenotype became common in the small cat population on the Isle of Man.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 3,
        "topics": [
          {
            "ref": "17.2(3)",
            "role": "primary"
          }
        ],
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 3,
          "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>three</i></b><i> from: </i> <i> </i>",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "<b>1</b>  inbreeding <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "<b>2</b>  low genetic diversity / small gene pool <b>;</b> <i> </i>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "<b>3</b>  founder effect / bottleneck <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "<b>4</b>  genetic drift <b>;</b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 5,
              "text": "<b>5</b>  tailless (cat) has a selective advantage / is selected for <b>; ora </b>",
              "numberedInMs": false
            },
            {
              "n": 6,
              "text": "<b>6</b>  tailless <b>allele</b> is dominant <b>; </b> <b> </b>",
